  us when  in reality they were curating black  dependency  they bragged about how they  were investing in our neighborhood when  we clearly don't see any fruits of the  so-called investment around here at all  in other words these liberals exploited  black pain for their own  personal  and professional  prestige  they never paid the price for the damage  they did  to our communities  we would have been way better off had  they never tried to help us in the first  place  that's a fact  now i'm seeing the very same thing here  with drill music and  the corporations and radio stations that  profit off this music  these corporate folks they're all doing  the same thing that these liberals do  they they come in  they take this music  they put it on the air  they glorify it  that's a part of our culture our are you  kidding me killing rappers you think  that's a part of our culture  these people make millions  off these lyrics and i know it's  millions because they pay these dirt  poor rappers millions for their lyrics  what dirt poor kid  in the hood is going to say no  what other options do these kids have  that gets them  wealth  insane wealth overnight  i don't hold these kids  totally responsible for their lyrics i  hold them responsible for the lyrics but  not totally responsible because  if it were not for these corporations  keeping the music alive and profiting  off of the dead bodies  then what we're seeing what we're  experiencing  we would not even be seeing it at all  i want to talk about this because  this really  fires me up this drill music is exactly  what i've been fighting against for 22  years i've been trying to teach kids  here in america the values in our hood  what values and principles are about  i've been saying to them how important  it is to take advantage of opportunities  and make the best of their lives  in the midst of poverty trying to let  them know that they can do it  and then here we are in the grasp of  this post-60 liberalism  and these bad policies  and we have to go against this drill  music that teaches the opposite values  and  i have to give eulogies for drill music  victims  it makes the work that we're doing  very difficult  so we need to expose these corporations  these radio djs  for what they truly are culture vultures  they feed off the black pain  that's what they're doing  they're they're they're feeding off  black pain culture vultures as for me  the work continues every single day my  team and i will never stop our work we  know we are doing the right thing we  know these corporations and radio  stations have all the money in the world  and will dismiss our complaints  let them  but we will never stop doing our work  the culture vultures promise death we  promote life  we promote doing it a better way  but not these culture vultures  they're only interested in the money  they don't care about black lives  they don't care about young black men  killing one another  use the word ops  and the n-word  as much as you want degrade women as  much as you want here take this money  we'll pay you over and over and over  again  why  because that's what culture vultures do  that's all i want to say about this  as i always say thank you fox for  another opportunity  to bring you my thoughts viewpoints and  opinions  to share with you  an america rooftop revelations  thank you to eli steele for producing  such a wonderful  show thank you to terrell  for filming  and as i always say  another rooftop revelation  and until tomorrow god bless you god  bless america  peace  you
 

